# Fills under tapered ink, 192x64, three shapes on paper at y 32, each filled and outlined in dark
# ink whose width varies. In every cell the fill shows solid inside the ink, with no paper hole and
# no ink over the middle.
# Cell 1 (x 32): a gold blob with stroke:p.ink,[2 8 2]: the ink is thin where the outline starts and
# ends and swells to about 8 px around the middle of its length.
# Cell 2 (x 96): a blue circle of radius 22 with stroke:p.ink,5 taper:.4: the ink is 5 px on the left
# and thins to a hairline at the seam on the right, where the circle's contour starts and ends.
# Cell 3 (x 160): a 44 px green square with stroke:p.ink,[2 6] taper:.3 and brush:dry(on:fill): the
# fill is broken into horizontal dry streaks with paper gaps, while the ink stays crisp and unbroken;
# the ink is a hairline along the left half of the top edge, from the seam at the top-left corner,
# and is thickest along the bottom.
# The .svg target uses profile:svg: cells 1 and 2 are a fill path under an ink path and match the
# PNG. Cell 3 is baked to a raster tile whose streaks fall in different places than the PNG's, as in
# brush/stack.
@target shapes/ink_fill.png 192x64
@target shapes/ink_fill.svg 192x64 profile:svg

use std/brushes { dry }

blob 24 at:32,32 fill:p.gold.2 stroke:p.ink,[2 8 2] name:listed
circle 22 at:96,32 fill:p.blue.2 stroke:p.ink,5 taper:.4 name:tapered
rect 44 at:160,32 fill:p.green.2 stroke:p.ink,[2 6] taper:.3 brush:dry(strength:.6 on:fill) name:brushed
